+  of the light curve's variance at the peak, so a low-amplitude sinusoid on top of red
+  noise can be coherent yet have low power. At least 34 `quiet` sources (19,554 files)
+  have periods of 0.10–2.2 d and amplitudes of 110–680 ppm. In each, the LS peak at that
+  period exceeds 20 times the local periodogram level in both halves of the year,
